    "content": {
      "component": "blog_article",
      "sharepoint_id": "75",
      "title": "Preventable Deaths: A Call to Action for Global Health and Well-being",
      "description": "",
      "date": "May 29, 2025",
      "read_time": "2 min read",
      "author": "Shafi Ullah",
      "isGlobal": true,
      "banner_image": {
        "fieldtype": "asset",
        "_local": "75-Banner.jpg"
      },
      "thumbnail": {
        "fieldtype": "asset"
      },
      "languages": [],
      "show_share": true,
      "show_similar": true,
      "similar_show_header": true,
      "category": "",
      "isFeatured": null,
      "body": [
        {
          "component": "rich_text",
          "content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) 3, which aims to ensure healthy lives and foster well-being for all, is of critical importance. Concerted efforts in recent decades have made significant headway in reducing maternal and infant mortality. According to "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "research",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK361904/",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", these advancements, saving millions of lives, are certainly cause for delight. However, this progress stands in stark contrast to an unacceptable reality: many people still die from illnesses that are treatable or avoidable. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "This issue extends beyond mere statistics, deeply affecting global equity and the shared responsibility of SDG 3. Understanding the reasons behind these unnecessary deaths, particularly among disadvantaged groups, is crucial for shaping effective responses. This article will discuss the key causes of this pressing issue and advocate for targeted, innovative action."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "SDG 3",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://www.globalgoals.org/goals/3-good-health-and-well-being/",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " defines \"preventable deaths\" to include those caused by tuberculosis and malaria, especially among mothers, infants, and young children, as well as problems related to pregnancy and delivery. A significant number of these deaths occur in low- and middle-income nations, highlighting profound global health inequalities. International health organizations like WHO and UNICEF assert that the continued occurrence of these deaths is even more unacceptable given the proven effectiveness of proper nutrition, clean water and sanitation, vaccination campaigns, and skilled birth attendance. Deficient health systems in many areas further exacerbate this "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "problem",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://australian.physio/inmotion/bridging-global-health-gaps",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A major contributing factor is the lack of adequate healthcare access. This encompasses insufficient healthcare facilities, a shortage of qualified nurses, doctors, and midwives, disrupted pharmaceutical and vaccine supply chains, and high costs that prevent poor families from affording treatment, according to "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "latest research",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://pjmr.org.pk/index.php/pjmr/article/view/843",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". Therefore, achieving universal health coverage and improving fundamental healthcare infrastructure are essential for reducing preventable deaths."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Beyond the clinic, this issue also impacts the socioeconomic fabric of communities. Poverty severely restricts access not only to medical care but also to secure housing and nutritious food. Lower levels of education are closely linked to poorer health outcomes, particularly for women and girls. Furthermore, long-standing gender discrimination can often limit women's ability to make decisions regarding their own and their children's health. These socioeconomic determinants of health impede progress towards the lofty goals of SDG 3, creating a cycle of vulnerability where preventable sickness and death regrettably become the norm."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The persistence of preventable deaths among women and children in impoverished communities reveals a significant lack of health equity. The primary causes are a combination of poverty and inequality, compounded by broken health systems that lack universal quality treatment. To solve this problem, we must improve primary healthcare systems and address socioeconomic issues through education, economic empowerment, and gender equality. Apathy in the face of this challenge robs millions of lives and unfulfilled potential, thereby undermining SDG 3. This is not merely a health crisis; it is a moral obligation that demands continuous and urgent global action."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
